18	// ---- Session handling rules: page controls via the confirm gate ------------------------------
19	//
20	// The console edits session rules through POST/PUT/DELETE /api/session/rules, all riskCredential
21	// and all behind the one-time confirmation gate. The ui2 page mirrors the Triage pattern rather
22	// than the Scope one: the confirm step mints the token, holds the exact minted call (method,
23	// path, bytes) in the bounded review map below, and renders a review sheet from those same
24	// bytes; the run form carries only the review id and token, and the run step dispatches the held
25	// call verbatim. Nothing typed after the review can change what is written, and a double-confirm
26	// cannot dispatch twice (LoadAndDelete).
27	//
28	// Add still dispatches through the wire API (POST with a body this page builds whole), and
29	// remove through DELETE; neither re-reads stored state, so the wire round-trip loses nothing.
30	//
31	// Toggle and edit do NOT go through the wire API. The served DTO carries no Action.Validity or
32	// Action.ExtensionSession (verified against sessionActionDto/actionToDto/actionsToModel), so a
33	// PUT of the served map silently drops both - the sheet's "everything else is kept unchanged"
34	// was false for rules carrying them. Those ops now merge at the DOMAIN level: a deep copy of
35	// the coordinator's stored rule (session.Coordinator.RuleSnapshot, one lock hold with the
36	// digest, extraction recompile like the persistence loader) has exactly the form-owned fields
37	// mutated (enabled; name, scope_tools), is validated with the engine's own session.ValidateRule
38	// at mint, and is installed by session.UpdateRuleIfUnchanged - the same compare-and-update the
39	// API's PUT uses, in one lock hold - followed by persistSessionRules in the API's ordering.
40	// The review entry holds the merged rule's domain marshal: those exact bytes are what
41	// session.RuleDigest binds, what the token covers, and what the sheet shows redacted, so
42	// what the operator sees is what installs. Per-action validity criteria render as stored
43	// (the sheet says so); extension_session and the credential carriers are withheld.
44	//
45	// expected_base is the session.RuleDigest of the rule at mint time (RuleSnapshot's half of the
46	// same lock hold); the check-and-swap runs inside one coordinator lock hold - a digest compared
47	// by the caller before a separate unconditional write would be a window, not a guard.
48	//
49	// The review map is bounded by ui2SessionRuleReviewCap with sweep-on-issue, the same shape the
50	// reviewer approved for Triage: enough for a few open tabs, small enough that a full map is a
51	// pileup to surface rather than paper over.
52	const ui2SessionRuleReviewCap = 8
53	
54	// ui2SessionRuleReview is one minted session-rule change held for review. It dies with ConfirmTTL
55	// so a stale review refuses alongside its token, and the run step spends it atomically.
56	type ui2SessionRuleReview struct {
57		token   string
58		method  string
59		url     string
60		body    []byte // wire ops: the exact minted call body, dispatched verbatim on run (nil for DELETE); domain ops: the merged rule's domain marshal, installed via compare-and-update
61		note    string // the success note the run step renders, written at mint time
62		expires time.Time
63		// domain marks a coordinator-level install (toggle/edit): the run step decodes body as a
64		// session.SessionRule and installs it with UpdateRuleIfUnchanged under expectedBase, rather
65		// than dispatching method+url+body through the API - the wire DTO drops Action.Validity and
66		// Action.ExtensionSession, so re-encoding would lose them. ruleID names the rule the swap
67		// targets; expectedBase is the RuleDigest the swap is preconditioned on.
68		domain       bool
69		ruleID       int64
70		expectedBase string
71	}
